# BUILD-23 — keeps the Docker build context small and prevents
# host-built artifacts (which may not match the container's platform)
# from being copied in instead of being rebuilt inside the image.

# VCS
.git/
.gitignore

# Dependencies (reinstalled inside the image)
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Build outputs (rebuilt inside the image)
dist/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
.next/
next-env.d.ts

# Secrets — never bake credentials into an image layer (SEC-DOCKER-1).
# Docker matches these patterns against the build-context root, so a bare ".env" only ever excluded the root file. The compose
# environment file (infrastructure/deployment/oci/.env) and operator backups next to it were therefore copied into the image by
# `COPY . .`. "**/" makes every pattern apply at any depth. Template files stay (".env.example" is tracked and harmless).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.env
**/*env-backup*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/.git-credentials
**/.netrc
**/.aws/
**/.ssh/
**/.gnupg/
# Operator evidence files written next to the compose file by the production discovery scripts
**/discovery-*.txt
**/rp12*.txt

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# OS / IDE
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Docs (not needed at runtime, keeps context lean)
docs/
